  "id": "cryostat",
  "term": "cryostat",
  "definition": "A cryostat is a device used to cut thin sections of frozen tissue for histology. In this context, it is part of cryo-sectioning, which can be difficult with fatty tissues because freezing-related artifacts may affect later image interpretation.",
